{"etag": "W/\"9ba2eafdcbb90402bc5abfe4b0f13ac8e23baf984b7c24341c9d85f641ff7fb6\"", "items": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/issues/2", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/issues/2/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/issues/2/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/issues/2/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/pull/2", "id": 5754214444, "node_id": "PR_kwDOUoOq6c8AAAABHO-Gbg", "number": 2, "title": "Listing prep p5", "user": {"login": "Kghaffari26", "id": 108359594, "node_id": "U_kgDOBnVvqg", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108359594?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26", "html_url": "https://github.com/Kghaffari26", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-10-08T01:12:15Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-08T01:12:57Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-08T01:12:57Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "OWNER", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/pulls/2", "html_url": "https://github.com/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/pull/2", "diff_url": "https://github.com/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/pull/2.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/Kghaffari26/real-estate-agent/pull/2.patch", "merged_at": "2026-10-08T01:12:56Z"}, "body": "Listing Prep P5 (SPEC_LISTING_PREP.md \u00a76, \u00a77): the report agent, its checks, the `reports` queue, the worker wiring, and the owner's follow-ups.\r\n\r\n## The report agent\r\n- **`agents/listing_prep/report.py`**: an `AgentLoop` (smart tier, 14 steps, $0.75) with the eleven read-only tools of \u00a76 over a JSON snapshot with no street address or names. Comparables and competing listings answer \"not licensed yet\" (P7). `evidence_gaps` reports the research left and the data gaps the report must state.\r\n- **The model writes the narrative only.** `assemble` builds the nine sections, methodology, gaps, sources and the not-an-appraisal disclaimer from code.\r\n- **Checks on `finish`**, in order:\r\n  1. Structure, item keys, no computed multiples, no promises, fair-housing rules (a new report scope: distances to schools allowed; ratings and \"school district\" not).\r\n  2. A fast-tier fair-housing reviewer. It fails closed: if it can't answer, the template is published.\r\n  3. The number guard: one retry, then the template.\r\n- **Template notice:** a template report says why it is one (review unavailable with the reviewer's reason, figures mismatched, research stopped early). The notice is in the report and in `reports.note`, shown at the top of the Desk's new Report card, which also requests and cancels reports. The full report view is P6.\r\n\r\n## Queue, worker and spend\r\n- **`reports` table**: `request_report`, `cancel_report`, team RLS, one queued or running report per property.\r\n- **Daily caps:** an `ai_spend` ledger records every report and photo analysis. `claim_report_job(team_cap, global_cap, reserve)` skips teams whose spend today plus a report's worst case would pass their cap, and claims nothing over the global cap. Defaults are $5 a team and $15 in all (repository variables), on top of the per-run cap ($2.50; at most 2 reports a run).\r\n- **Clean worker exit:** the worker ends green with a warning annotation when its Supabase secrets are missing, the URL isn't https, the key is rejected, the migrations aren't applied or the host is unreachable. Other errors still fail the run.\r\n\r\n## Evals\r\n- Six fictional fixture properties.\r\n- `TEMPLATE_REPORTS` is free, scores 1.0 and joins the PR gate.\r\n- **`report-agent-eval.yml`** runs the live `REPORT_AGENT` eval ($2.50 cap, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` only) and uploads the trajectories as an artifact. Add the **`live-eval`** label to this PR to run it. Committing the recordings then turns on the replay test.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n- pytest: tools, every check, the loop end to end on a scripted model, the worker (caps, notes, config exits), and the workflow contracts.\r\n- PGlite RLS for `reports` and the caps.\r\n- e2e for the Report card, axe-clean.\r\n- A report run on the real stack in `desk-db`: green on 716f529.\r\n\r\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)", "closed_by": {"login": "Kghaffari26", "id": 108359594, "node_id": "U_kgDOBnVvqg", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108359594?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26", "html_url": "https://github.com/Kghaffari26", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://